    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="c8604545-7aa8-5ea1-a059-b4ba371f8bda" activityNameId="796acc3b-9bfd-5c44-8eeb-c842fadbf72a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Operation, maintenance, railway track</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Operation, maintenance, railway track
Inventory for a conventional gravel track bedding. Expenditures due to tunnel construction and bridge construction have been taken into account, according to the share of tunnels and bridges in the Swiss rail network.;
UUID: c144a4d4-ac3f-3a68-8a46-256d1c446b2a
The inventory includes the energy consumption required for the operation of the rail track as well as the operation of tunnels. The use and emissions to soil of herbicides (weed control) and lubricates (point maintenance) are taken into account. Also land transformation and occupation are accounted for.
Location: Data refers to average conditions in Switzerland and a specific conditions in Germany
Technology: Data represents current technologies
Time period: Rail length is based on current statistical data (2000). The material consumption represents a situation in the early 1990ties and a recent high speed track in Germany
Production volume: na
Sampling: national statistics and literature studies 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_c144a4d4-ac3f-3a68-8a46-256d1c446b2a.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
